    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW21jZfxe5AmskoMP3AYBnVbr)_\n\nStacked on #49 (which sits on #48 and #45). Merge in that order; GitHub retargets each PR as its base merges.\n\nBefore: the module, doc, options and commands were `sp-splash*`, and the doc gave every face its own sub-heading, with more faces defined and explained in other sections.\n\nAfter:\n- `sp-splash` is `sp-dashboard`: `libraries/modules/tooling/sp-dashboard.el`, `docs/tangles/tooling/sp-dashboard.org`, the load lists in `init.el`, `sp-gui-only-set` in `early-init.el`, `sp-config-profiles.el`, `docs/main.org`, `docs/load-order.org` and `conditional-loading.org`/`.el`. Every `sp-splash-*` option, face, function and key map is now `sp-dashboard-*` (for example `M-x sp-dashboard-screen`). The buffer is still `Dashboard`. `initback` and the open entries of older CHANGELOG sections keep the old name, since they are history.\n- In `sp-dashboard.org` there is one `* Faces` heading with no sub-headings: a list explaining all twelve faces (title, header, footer, menu, box, image, art, banner, three accents, focus) and one source block that defines them all. The defaces moved out of the art, palette, menu and mode sections into that block, and the `.el` has them in the same place so the doc still tangles to the same text.\n\nChecked in headless Emacs 29.3: the module loads under the new name, the dashboard draws, TAB moves between buttons, and a theme change recolours the art. The doc's blocks tangle to the `.el`.\n\nYour custom settings: any `sp-splash-*` variable you set in your own config (for example the art offsets) needs the new `sp-dashboard-` prefix.\n\nLabelled `correction` as asked.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01T2BcMQ3qdNUiW5oZRLQRsG)_",
